munity": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Klaus73", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVMBj9Hc.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/alx/status/2101056612073156739", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "President Trump was BANNED from Social Platforms -  Yet It is NOT OK for Trump to BAN Lying Propaganda Outlets - CNN-Dem News, MSNOW, Politico -   Hypocrisy Runs Deep w Liberals & The Globalists Who OWN Them", "last_comment_created": 1789850719880, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 6, "score_up": 203, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": [{"width": 1320, "heightRatio": 55, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HShz2oaacAEMwao.jpg", "height": 735}], "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 656, "created": 1789765906000, "id": "2101056612073156739", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2096598301919576064/uz6cIRc2_normal.jpg", "displayName": "ALX \ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\uddf8", "username": "alx"}, "content": "I don\u2019t care if CNN, MSNBC and Politico are banned from The White House.\n\nGoing to The White House is a privilege, not a right. They can report news anywhere.\n\nTrump was banned from Twitter, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, etc\u2026 they said nothing \u2014 even worse they cheered it on.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 19575}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVMCrpFp", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 19, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8845769, "raw_content": "Regulatory costs by president.  Biden v. Trump:\n\nBiden administration (2021\u20132025) -\n\nCumulative new-rule costs exceeded $1.8 trillion\u2014the highest of any recent administration. 2024 alone added $1.4 trillion, the single costliest year on record. Large shares came from EPA vehicle-emissions and energy rules. Some studies put the lifetime burden near $47,000 per household. \n\nTrump first term (2017\u20132021) -\n\nNet reduction. Executive Order 13771 produced roughly $150 billion in scored savings plus additional cuts outside the order. One analysis found about $11,000 in present-value savings per household. \n\nTrump second term (2025\u2013present) -\n\n2025 produced $130 billion in net savings\u2014the most deregulatory calendar year recorded. Through mid-2026, finalized rules under a new one-in/ten-out order have generated more than $1.1 trillion in scored cost reductions, bringing the administration\u2019s running total near $1.2 trillion. Congressional Review Act repeals of late Biden rules added smaller extra savings. \n\nBroader annual estimates of the entire existing regulatory stock (not just new rules) range from $2.15 trillion (Competitive Enterprise Institute) to over $3 trillion (National Association of Manufacturers).\n\n", "author": "KuzoKevin", "created": 1789872728048, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "cyberrigger", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Inflation is lower under Trump, and so are regulatory costs.  That saves us all money and encourages economic growth.", "last_comment_created": 1789892278229, "content": "<p>Regulatory costs by president.  Biden v. Trump:</p>\n<p>Biden administration (2021\u20132025) -</p>\n<p>Cumulative new-rule costs exceeded $1.8 trillion\u2014the highest of any recent administration. 2024 alone added $1.4 trillion, the single costliest year on record. Large shares came from EPA vehicle-emissions and energy rules. Some studies put the lifetime burden near $47,000 per household.</p>\n<p>Trump first term (2017\u20132021) -</p>\n<p>Net reduction. Executive Order 13771 produced roughly $150 billion in scored savings plus additional cuts outside the order. One analysis found about $11,000 in present-value savings per household.</p>\n<p>Trump second term (2025\u2013present) -</p>\n<p>2025 produced $130 billion in net savings\u2014the most deregulatory calendar year recorded. Through mid-2026, finalized rules under a new one-in/ten-out order have generated more than $1.1 trillion in scored cost reductions, bringing the administration\u2019s running total near $1.2 trillion. Congressional Review Act repeals of late Biden rules added smaller extra savings.</p>\n<p>Broader annual estimates of the entire existing regulatory stock (not just new rules) range from $2.15 trillion (Competitive Enterprise Institute) to over $3 trillion (National Association of Manufacturers).</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 4, "score_up": 19, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVMCqien", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 52, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8845301, "raw_content": "", "author": "ColonelKlink", "created": 1789852663735, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.dailymail.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVMCqien.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.dailymail.com/news/article-16144509/Teen-gang-jailed-stabbing-boy-death-McDonalds.html", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Mexican/black \"teen\" gangs murdering in London now?", "last_comment_created": 1789852663735, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 52, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "Two teenagers have been jailed over the killing of a 17-year-old boy after stabbing him outside a McDonald's restaurant in London and sharing pictures of their bloodied hands online.\u00a0", "large_image": "i8cRoNdtnm9dLtjT.png", "title": "Gang stabbed boy to death outside McDonald's"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}], "status": true}